      "text": "## 1. Object identification\n- This is a small **EDIT** of the current Retro Desk Fan (v2). Everything stays untouched: the fan body, rotor, cage, buttons, speed pill, spin physics, airflow shape/count/width, and the soft blob shadow under the base.\n- The request is that the **airflow ribbons must not cast or receive any shadow** on the fan, the floor or each other. They should look like pure light-blue, unlit streaks, as in Reference 1.\n- Certain:\n  - The ribbons use an unlit `ShaderMaterial`, so they cannot be shaded by lights.\n  - The only way they can show shadow is through the shadow-map pass, if a mesh is flagged `castShadow`/`receiveShadow`.\n- Assumed: the host scene enables shadow maps and may flag every mesh in the model as a shadow caster. This is the likely source of the unwanted shadow. It is also why the fix must be applied to the ribbons explicitly and re-asserted at runtime.\n- Assumed: the motion-blur disc (`motionBlur`) is a transparent effect like the airflow. It should also be excluded from shadows, otherwise it throws a faint cream disc shadow when the fan spins.\n\n## 2. Exact component inventory (what is affected)\n- 48 airflow ribbon meshes, `airflow_0` … `airflow_47`.\n- 1 motion-blur disc, `motionBlur`, in the rotor group.\n- Not affected:\n  - Base, stand, neck, housing, blades, hub and cage keep `castShadow = true` and `receiveShadow = true`.\n  - The fake blob shadow plane `shadow` stays as the ground shadow. It is the fan's shadow, not the airflow's.\n\n## 3. Geometry and architecture\nNo geometry changes. The ribbon paths, tube resolution (40 × 4), slots, swirl, hooks and respawn logic stay exactly as they are.\n\nRequired flag rules for every ribbon mesh and for `motionBlur`:\n- `castShadow = false`\n- `receiveShadow = false`\n- Do not set `customDepthMaterial` or `customDistanceMaterial`, so no shadow pass can pick them up.\n- Keep `frustumCulled = false`, `depthWrite = false` and `transparent = true`, as now.\n\n## 4. Scale and proportions\nUnchanged (1 unit = 1 m). The airflow column width, reach and bounding box are exactly as in v2.\n\n## 5. Colors and materials\n- Ribbon color is unchanged: `#86C7DE` fading to `#B7E0EE`, normal blending.\n- Material stays an unlit `ShaderMaterial` with no `lights: true` and no shadow chunks, so lighting can never darken it.\n- The ribbon alpha window, fade-in and opacity formula stay the same.\n- `motionBlur` stays a `MeshBasicMaterial` (unlit), cream `#F2E8DA`, with opacity driven by speed as now.\n\n## 6. Build strategy (changes only)\n1. In the patch layer, where the ribbons are created, set `mesh.castShadow = false` and `mesh.receiveShadow = false` on each ribbon right after creating it.\n2. Do the same for `root.getObjectByName('motionBlur')`.\n3. Re-assert the flags at runtime:\n   - On the first `update()` call, run one `root.traverse` that forces both flags to `false` on every object whose name starts with `airflow_` or equals `motionBlur`.\n   - This covers a host that sets `castShadow = true` on all meshes after the model is built.\n   - After that, ribbons that are rebuilt on respawn only swap `geometry`, so the flags persist. No per-frame work is needed.\n4. Leave the existing `castShadow` and `receiveShadow` on the fan parts alone. Only the airflow and the blur disc are changed.\n5. No new geometry, materials or textures, so the triangle budget is unchanged (~46k total).\n\n## 7. Interactions and animation\n- None changed. Speed modes, knob and button clicks, inertia and fade-out behave as in v2.\n- Visual result at every speed: the blue streaks appear with no dark patches on the fan or ground and no ribbon-shaped shadows. The only ground shadow is the soft blob under the base.\n\n## 8. Assumptions and open questions\n- **Interpretation used:** \"airflow shadow\" means a real shadow-map shadow cast by the ribbons (and the blur disc). Both are removed.\n- **Blur disc:** it is also removed from shadows. If you want the spinning blade ghost to keep its shadow, tell me and I will leave it flagged.\n- **Blob shadow:** the soft elliptical shadow under the base stays, since it belongs to the fan. If you meant that blob, tell me and I will remove or shrink it instead.\n- **Reference 1 detail:** its ground shadow includes scribbly airflow streaks. This is deliberately not reproduced, in line with your request.",
