      "text": "## 1. Object identification\n- This is a small **EDIT** of the current Retro Desk Fan (v3). Everything else stays untouched: the fan body, rotor, cage, buttons, speed pill, spin inertia, no-shadow flags, and the blob shadow under the base.\n- Only the **airflow motion and shape** change. The user wants three things:\n  1. The airflow must **not spin or swirl**. The streaks must be straight and parallel, with no rotation around the fan axis.\n  2. All streaks must **spawn at the same time**, as one synchronized wave from the whole fan face. No ribbon should be out of phase with the others.\n  3. The airflow must be **the same width as the fan**: a straight column of cage width (Ø 0.316 m) that does not fan out.\n- Causes in v3:\n  - `swirl = 0.6·s` rotates the paths around the axis.\n  - The shader wiggle uses `sin` on X and `cos` on Y. Together these make a circular motion that reads as spinning.\n  - Each ribbon has its own staggered phase `frac(i·0.381966)` and its own respawn time.\n  - `k = 0.08 + 0.25·s` and `k2` widen the column with distance.\n  - The tail hooks and wiggle push streaks outside the fan width.\n\n## 2. Exact component inventory (airflow only)\n- The pool stays at **48 ribbons**, `airflow_0` … `airflow_47`. The active counts stay `[0, 16, 32, 48]` for Off / Low / Med / High.\n- The start slots stay on the fan face (golden-angle, uniform-area). The slot radius stays `0.150·sqrt(frac((i+0.5)·0.618034))`, so slots cover the full disc and the outer ring reaches 0.150 m.\n- **Removed:**\n  - the swirl,\n  - the radial expansion (`k`, `k2`),\n  - the tail hooks (0 hooks, previously about 25%),\n  - the per-ribbon random path wiggle,\n  - the per-ribbon staggered phase.\n- Kept: the thickness mix (30% at 0.005 m, 70% at 0.0022 m) and the unlit shader color.\n\n## 3. Geometry and architecture\n**Path (6 control points)**\n- Every ribbon is a straight line along +Z.\n- Point i (t = i/5): `x = x0`, `y = 0.37 + y0`, `z = 0.13 + reach·t`.\n- `x0 = r·cosθ` and `y0 = r·sinθ`, with `r` and `θ` fixed from the slot.\n- The jitter on respawn is reduced to ±0.004 m in radius and ±0.05 rad in angle.\n  - The radius is clamped to ≤ 0.155 m, so the column never exceeds the cage radius.\n- No angle change along the ribbon, so there is no spiral.\n- No radial change along the ribbon, so the width is constant.\n- Column cross-section: a disc of Ø 0.31 m at every distance, matching the cage Ø 0.316 m.\n- Y clamp ≥ 0.03 is kept as a safety net (it never triggers, since the lowest point is 0.37 − 0.155 = 0.215).\n\n**Mesh resolution**\n- Unchanged: 40 tubular × 4 radial. The triangle count is flat at about 15k.\n\n**Shader (edit)**\n- Remove the Y wiggle (the `cos` term), which caused the circular motion.\n- Keep at most a tiny X-only ripple.\n  - Set the amplitude to `uAmp = 0.002 + 0.003·s` (max 0.005 m).\n  - The streaks then breathe a little but stay inside the fan width and show no rotation.\n  - Alternatively set `uAmp = 0` for perfectly rigid streaks (default: the tiny ripple).\n- Keep the moving-window alpha and the fade-in at the start.\n\n**Synchronized spawn**\n- Use **one global phase** `P` (0…1) for all ribbons:\n  - `P += dt·rate`, with `rate = 0.3 + 1.2·s`.\n  - Every ribbon sets `uHead = P·1.35`, with no per-ribbon offset.\n- When `P` wraps past 1 (`P -= 1`), **rebuild all ribbons in the same frame**.\n  - Each gets a new jitter and the current `reach`, so the whole wave restarts together from the fan face.\n- When the fan starts from Off (`s` rises above 0.01 from 0), reset `P = 0` so the first wave leaves the fan at once.\n- Ribbons that become active on a mode change join the current global phase. They fade in over 0.25 s and so are in step with the others.\n- Each wave then looks like a flat wall of air the size of the fan, pushed out at once.\n\n## 4. Scale and proportions\n- Unit scale is unchanged (1 unit = 1 m).\n- Column diameter: **0.31 m** at every distance, equal to the fan width, with a constant cross-section.\n- Reach (same for all ribbons): `reach = 0.4 + 0.8·max(s, 0.2)`.\n  - Low: about 0.6 m.\n  - Med: about 0.85 m.\n  - High: 1.2 m.\n- Bounding box of the airflow: X ±0.155, Y 0.215–0.525, Z 0.13 up to 1.33 at High.\n- The camera needs no change. The column is narrower than in v2, so it is easier to frame.\n\n## 5. Colors and materials\n- Unchanged: `#86C7DE` fading to `#B7E0EE`, unlit `ShaderMaterial`, transparent, `depthWrite` off.\n- Opacity stays `op = (0.35 + 0.55·s)·min(1, 6s)`.\n- The `0.75` gain for center slots (r < 0.04) and the `0.85` gain for thin ribbons are kept, so overlapping streaks do not form a bright core.\n- `castShadow` and `receiveShadow` stay `false` on all ribbons and `motionBlur`.\n\n## 6. Build strategy (changes only)\n1. Remove the old airflow meshes from the previous patch and rebuild them in a new patch. Dispose the old geometries and materials.\n2. Rewrite `rebuild(r)`: straight path, fixed slot, small jitter, radius clamp, no hook, no swirl, no expansion.\n3. Change the vertex shader: drop the Y wiggle and use the small X-only ripple.\n4. Replace the per-ribbon phase `r.p` with the global `P` in `update()`:\n   - advance `P` once per frame,\n   - on wrap, loop over all 48 ribbons and rebuild them,\n   - set the same `uHead` on all of them.\n5. Set the `castShadow = false` and `receiveShadow = false` flags on the new meshes, and keep the first-update re-assert.\n6. Do not touch the fan, rotor, cage, UI, blob shadow or click logic.\n\n## 7. Interactions and animation\n- Triggers are unchanged: the 4 buttons and the knob click.\n- Per mode (driven by `s = ω/32`, so it ramps with the blade inertia):\n\n| Mode | Active ribbons | Wave rate (waves/s) | Reach | Column width |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Off | 0 (fade out ~0.8 s) | — | — | — |\n| Low | 16 | ~0.6 | ~0.6 m | 0.31 m |\n| Med | 32 | ~1.0 | ~0.85 m | 0.31 m |\n| High | 48 | ~1.5 | 1.2 m | 0.31 m |\n\n- Ribbons beyond the active count still fade out smoothly.\n- There is no rotation of the airflow at any speed. The blades alone spin.\n\n## 8. Assumptions and open questions\n- **\"Spawn at the same time\" interpretation:** all ribbons start from the fan face in one synchronized wave, with no staggering. If you meant that airflow should appear only once the fan is spinning, that already happens (it fades in as `s` rises).\n- **Width:** it equals the cage Ø 0.316 m, with no fan-out. If you want it slightly wider at the far end, tell me and I will add 10–15% expansion.\n- **Hooks removed:** the curl at the tail of some streaks is gone, because it left the fan width. I can bring it back if you want it.\n- **Ripple:** a tiny sideways ripple (≤ 5 mm) remains for life. I can set it to zero for rigid straight streaks.\n- **Pulsing look:** a single synchronized wave may look like pulses. If it feels too mechanical, I can add a small stagger (e.g. ±10% of the cycle) while keeping the same spawn plane.",
